{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-server-database-1-b-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-3","surface":"server","area":"server/database-1","refs":["F-server-321","F-server-322"],"severity":"S3","title":"A workout offer set to give the days by itself can quietly not give them, with no reason shown","what":"When the owner picks 'Give the days by themselves', the admin app says the days are added to the member's plan at once. If the member reaches the target on a day with no running gym plan, the automatic give fails silently. Nothing records why: the member just sits as 'Ready for reward' like on a desk-given offer. It is tried again only when the member next opens their offer card in the app, not when the desk renews the plan. So an owner who trusts the automatic setting can believe the reward went when it did not.","expected":"When the automatic give cannot happen, the server keeps a reason (no running plan) that the offer list shows on that member, and it tries again when a new plan is saved, not only when the member opens the app.","evidence":["supabase/migrations/0025_workout_offer.sql:625-636","supabase/migrations/0025_workout_offer.sql:280-281","supabase/migrations/0025_workout_offer.sql:492-500","supabase/migrations/0025_workout_offer.sql:389-390","apps/dashboard/src/crm/shop/OffersSection.tsx:296-298"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"auto-reward-fail-no-reason","who":"owners running an automatic workout offer","how_often":"when a member qualifies between two plans","fix_line":"Save a 'could not give: no running plan' note on the member's offer row, show it in the list, and retry when a plan is saved","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
